cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use spoligotyper, please cite it as below, together with BBTools."
title: "spoligotyper: in silico spoligotyping of Mycobacterium tuberculosis complex genomes"
type: software
abstract: >-
  spoligotyper finds the 43 spacers of the direct repeat (DR) locus of Mycobacterium tuberculosis complex genomes in
  sequencing reads (fastq) or genome assemblies (fasta), using Seal from BBTools. It reports the spoligotype as
  binary, octal and hexadecimal codes, and as an SB number from the Mbovis.org database of spoligotype patterns.
